# CognifyAI frontend configuration. Copy to .env and adjust if needed.
#
# Read this before editing: the value does not behave the way a runtime .env file implies. It is
# `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`, so Next.js inlines it into the emitted client bundle at BUILD time; the
# `frontend/Dockerfile` builder stage passes it as a build ARG and compose declares no `args`, so
# an image built from this repo already contains the default below. Changing this file after the
# build changes nothing the browser runs; see the Configuration section of README.md.

# The one variable production code reads: the `API_BASE_URL` constants in `src/lib/api/client.ts`,
# `src/lib/api/events.ts` and `src/lib/api/reports.ts`, each falling back to this same default,
# and `next.config.ts`, which builds the Content-Security-Policy's `connect-src` from its origin.
# To point the UI at a different backend you must rebuild.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000/api/v1
